WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
good afternoon i'm assistant sheriff  andrew walsh and i'm here today to brief  you on the additional details as we know  them today about the officer-involved  shooting that took place on tuesday  october 12 2021.  this is officer-involved shooting number  eight for 2021 it's fatal event number  five  at the same time last year we had 16  officer-involved shootings eight of  which were fatal  this event was initiated by an assault  and battery with a firearm at 0-9-33  hours on october 12 2021  the address of the original call was in  the 5600 block of east lake mead  the officer-involved shooting occurred  near the intersection of sloan lane and  east charleston boulevard las vegas  nevada 89156  which is located in the southeast area  command and you can see that area  depicted on the map on the screen to my  left  the involved officer in this incident is  officer ramon highstand  ramon is 35 years old and he's been with  the lvmpd since 2014.  in this incident officer high stand was  armed with a cult le carbine 223 caliber  rifle equipped with a tactical light  and the investigation revealed he fired  eight rounds during this incident  orvis high stand is assigned to the  community policing division which is  within the community i'm sorry which is  within the southeast area command  and the suspect in this incident was  identified as mario lawrence martinez  he was a 43 year old hispanic male adult  he was 5 foot 10 and he weighed 260  pounds and he was pictured on the screen  to my left  in this incident martinez was armed with  a semi-automatic  s-c-c-y nine-millimeter handgun and the  investigation revealed he fired five  rounds during this incident two of those  rounds were fired while martinez was  kidnapping the victim from her apartment  and the rest of the rounds were fired at  the officer-involved shooting scene  had martinez survived he would have been  charged with kidnapping with a deadly  weapon attempted murder five counts of  attempted murder on a police officer  home invasion burglary with a firearm  and shooting into an occupied structure  and the details of the officer-involved  shooting are as follows  on tuesday october 25  tuesday october 12 2021 the lvmpd  dispatch center received a call from a  citizen reporting a shooting in a  four-plex apartment building located in  the 5600 block of east lake mead  boulevard the caller also stated that  the shooting was related to a domestic  violence incident  officers arrived and contacted a man in  front of the apartments the man  explained to the officers that this  apartment is where he and his girlfriend  live and he went on to explain how his  girlfriend's ex-boyfriend mario lawrence  martinez had been harassing them  he told officers that martinez came over  and fired shots before kicking in the  front door of the apartment  martinez entered the apartment and  forcibly removed his girlfriend  threatening her with a handgun  martinez attempted to leave the area  using the female's victim's vehicle  however her vehicle had a dead battery  martinez then forced the victim to walk  with him away from the apartment  building  patrol officers were able to determine  that martinez was likely heading to his  residence which was not far from the  lake mead address  a description of martinez and the victim  was broadcast to all officers in the  area  at approximately 10 50 a.m patrol  officers saw martinez and the victim  walking in the area of charleston  boulevard and sloan lane  officers tried to get martinez to  release the victim and asked him to  surrender  martinez failed to comply with the  officer's commands and began moving away  while holding the victim at gunpoint and  walked into a busy shopping center  parking lot  martinez attempted to steal a car that  was in a restaurant drive-thru and  martinez was unsuccessful in that  attempt and he also tried to steal two  other vehicles in the parking lot those  attempts were also unsuccessful  he then forced the victim to walk into a  grocery store with him while he was  still holding her at gunpoint and waving  the gun in the air  martinez made his way through the  grocery store and eventually exited the  store into the rear alley  throughout martinez's movements officers  followed and were in close proximity to  him and the victim  there was an unoccupied box truck which  you see in the picture to my left parked  to the rear of the grocery store  martinez shot out the window of that  vehicle and he attempted to steal it and  attempted to force the victim into it  he was unable to start the truck and  force the victim to walk with him  westbound in the alley towards sloan  lane while all this was happening  responding officers were setting up  containment around the shopping center  and as martinez was making his way  westbound toward sloan a team of  officers was already posted in the alley  which included officer ramon high stand  as martinez reached the sidewalk on the  east side of sloan lane he pointed his  firearm at officers  the victim then took this opportunity to  break away from martinez and officer  heist and then fired his rifle at  martinez striking him causing him to  fall to the ground when martinez fell to  the ground he began firing shots from  his handgun toward the officers officer  high stand returned fire and then  martinez stopped shooting officers moved  in to render aid however martinez was  pronounced deceased at the scene by  medical personnel and now we're going to  show you some body-worn camera footage  and we're also going to show you some  surveillance footage that we've  recovered so far during this from this  event  so this is video from the fast food  drive-through you can see martinez  wearing the blue shirt and there's the  victim standing behind him as he  attempts to gain entry into that vehicle  while holding the gun  and then what you'll see shortly is  martinez walks back towards that vehicle  and then he points his firearm  downrange in the parking lot at  responding officers to the  to this parking lot area  so you can see it's a crowded parking  lot  suspect forcibly holding the victim  and in this next video  what you're going to see is you can see  the victim and the suspect walking  towards this white suv that's pulling  down the  lane  the suspect drags the victim to the  passenger side of the vehicle attempts  to gain entry but the driver of the  vehicle is able to speed away  and it's at this point  where martinez takes the victim and  drags her into the supermarket  so the next  segment of this you'll see  the suspect and the victim entered the  store you can see  the firearm  and in here the suspect and the victim  are circled  and you see an officer using shopping  carts to block  the exit  and you see other officers in the right  of the screen  and then this is after  the suspect was unsuccessful in  stealing the box truck  he's going to come walking into view  here in a second  and you can see how he's holding the  victim at gunpoint using her as a shield  and this is in the alley as i described  earlier walking westbound towards sloane  and this is body one camera footage  from officer high stand  so the area you want to pay attention to  is along the wall  you'll get a glimpse of the  suspect and the victim  okay  [Music]  and this video that you're going to see  now is from the air unit  so again walking westbound  in the alley  okay  so slow down you see  she gets to walk away he raises the  firearm towards the officers and for  obvious reasons we're not going to show  the rest of that event  and that concludes this briefing  yeah obviously you see the drive-through  uh no calls from the people in the  drive-through  no calls we have calls from the  albertsons but no calls from  folks outside the second vehicle that  drives off no calls so you know people  should call us when they see something  like that i mean it's kind of sad when  you see a victim being dragged around at  gunpoint we don't get more calls than we  got we got some but not the amount that  you would think we got  do you know if martinez has any previous  history of  so as always in these press briefings we  tell you you can get their criminal  history from records  but between this  and this incident we don't know that  there's any history of domestic violence  between him and the victim  yes  she had some marks  from him holding her and she had an  injury to the back of her head which she  said was caused by the suspect  thankfully no and i appreciate you  asking  was this situation just because it was  just a moving scene from place to place  how dangerous was that for your officers  to try to make sure that they weren't  shooting someone in the background yeah  it's a great question i'm glad you asked  it because it really gives people an  indication of what  especially in our community what their  police department and what their  officers trained for and what they're  capable of  i think in this incident you know it's  it's really a  nightmare scenario of a mobile hostage  situation  but thankfully  the citizen  that was kidnapped was not hurt and  thankfully none of our officers were  hurt and no other citizens were hurt you  know the loss of life obviously in any  situation is sad and tragic for the  family members of that person involved  but in this situation the suspect  dictated the actions of the officers and  there was little left for us to do  all right thank you very much  you

